dsh-plugin-branchpoint README · What it does：- Adds a fork icon to `conversation.session.header.actions`, next to the branch title.
- Loads up to six older pages of session history when the prompt is outside the current window.
- Auto-detects splittable units in the branch:
  - sections with numbered tasks («Практика 2», «Задания», «Упражнения»);
  - substantive theory sections («Шаг 1. …», «Инструмент: …»);
  - the whole branch as a fallback.
- Opens a picker: task sections first with their task count, then theory sections, then **«Разобрать»** — formulas, functions, code fragments and libraries that matter but are not the topic itself. Each row has a one-line preview.
- Builds a scoped digest for the chosen unit:
  - the topic name from the first real request;
  - only that section's numbered tasks/questions — no other sections, no context block;
  - formulas stay in their original LaTeX (`$\log_2 32$`), so DSH renders them with KaTeX exactly as in the main branch; the readable form (`log₂(32)`) is used only for one-line previews in the picker;
  - one short mode line: «Не решай за меня — жди мои ответы».
- Keeps **«Вся ветка»** for the old full summary: goal, all topics, all tas

dsh-plugin-branchpoint README · How it works：- `lib/index.js` is a minimal host half (`name`, empty `apply`).
- `lib/client.js`:
  - `inject = ['slots', 'uiWorkspace', 'sessions']`;
  - registers in `conversation.session.header.actions`;
  - reads `ctx.sessions.binding(sessionId).eventSource`;
  - `entriesToTurns` and `entriesToTools` parse messages and tool calls;
  - `loadOlderHistory` pages older history (max 6 pages, 12 s);
  - `collectUnits` splits assistant answers into Markdown or bold headings (ignoring headings inside code fences) and detects numbered task blocks; `collectConcepts` finds formulas, functions, code fragments and imported libraries;
  - `buildUnitDigest` renders only the chosen section and keeps formulas as original LaTeX; `readableMath` is used only for one-line picker previews; `buildDigest` still renders the full branch;
  - the picker is a React portal (`react-dom`) with Escape/backdrop close;
  - `createBranch` uses `ctx.uiWorkspace.openWorkspace` to capture the new session id and `prepareDraft` to fill its composer;
  - `nextBranchNumber` numbers branches per parent; `markMain` renames the root chat to `🌳 …` once and pins it;
  - the parent id and unit
